# Neovim Configuration Rules

## Code Style
- Use 2 spaces for indentation in Lua files
- Prefer explicit local variables over globals
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Keep functions small and focused (max 30 lines)

## Lua Patterns
- Use `local function` instead of `function` for file-local functions
- Prefer `require()` over `vim.cmd()` when possible
- Use `vim.api.nvim_*` functions for buffer/window operations
- Organize code with clear separation of concerns

## Plugin Configuration
- Group related plugin configurations together
- Use lazy loading when appropriate
- Document complex configurations with comments
- Prefer declarative configuration over imperative

## Error Handling
- Always check if required modules exist before using them
- Use `pcall()` for operations that might fail
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Gracefully degrade when optional features are unavailable

## Performance
- Use `vim.schedule()` for async operations
- Avoid expensive operations in autocommands
- Cache results when appropriate
- Profile code when performance is critical

## Documentation
- Document all public functions with clear descriptions
- Include usage examples for complex functions
- Explain non-obvious logic with inline comments
- Keep documentation up to date with code changes


